{"turn": 2, "role": "tool", "result": "**[TERM SHEET --- CONSTRUCTION-TO-MINI-PERMANENT LOAN]{.underline}**\n\n**The Piedmont at Brightleaf** **601 and 615 Foster Street, Durham, North Carolina 27701**\n\n**NON-BINDING EXCEPT AS SET FORTH IN SECTIONS 22 AND 23 HEREOF**\n\n**Date:** January 10, 2025 **Bank Internal Loan Number:** CRE-2025-0342\n\nPrepared by **Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A.**, Commercial Real Estate Lending Division, 215 South Tryon Street, 18th Floor, Charlotte, North Carolina 28202.\n\nThis Term Sheet sets forth the proposed terms and conditions under which Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A. (\\\"Lender\\\") is prepared to provide construction-to-mini-permanent loan financing to Harborview Capital Partners LLC (\\\"Borrower\\\") for the development of the mixed-use project known as The Piedmont at Brightleaf, located at 601 and 615 Foster Street, Durham, North Carolina 27701. Except as expressly set forth in Sections 22 and 23 hereof, this Term Sheet does not constitute a binding commitment or obligation on the part of the Lender to make the proposed Loan or on the part of the Borrower to accept the proposed Loan.\n\n**[Section 1 --- Parties]{.underline}**\n\n**1.1 Lender. Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A.**, a nationally chartered savings bank organized and existing under the laws of the United States, regulated by the Office of the Comptroller of the Currency. The principal office of the Lender is located at 215 South Tryon Street, 18th Floor, Charlotte, North Carolina 28202.\n\n**Relationship Manager:** David Forsythe, Senior Vice President, Commercial Real Estate Lending.\n\n**Lender\\'s Counsel: Ashford, Cromdale Consulting & Laine LLP, 411 South Tryon Street, Suite 2800, Charlotte, North Carolina 28202. Lead Partner: Katharine \\\"Kate\\\" Drummond. Associate: Marcus Webb.**\n\n**1.2 Borrower. Harborview Capital Partners LLC**, a North Carolina limited liability company, organized and existing under the laws of the State of North Carolina, with the North Carolina Secretary of State File Number 1923847, formed on March 14, 2019. The principal office of the Borrower is located at 400 West Main Street, Suite 310, Durham, North Carolina 27701.\n\nThe membership interests in the Borrower are held as follows:\n\n> • **Elena Vasquez-Torres** --- 62% membership interest (Managing Member)\n>\n> • **Brightleaf Investors Group LLC** --- 28% membership interest (a North Carolina limited liability company; NC Secretary of State File No. 2045612; Managing Member: Thomas R. Chen)\n>\n> • **Reginald K. Osei** --- 10% membership interest\n\n**Borrower\\'s Counsel:** Calloway & Strauss PLLC, 324 Blackwell Street, Suite 200, Durham, North Carolina 27701. Lead Partner: Jonathan F. Ngo.\n\n**1.3 Guarantors.** The following individuals shall serve as guarantors of the Loan (each, a \\\"Guarantor\\\" and collectively, the \\\"Guarantors\\\"):\n\n> • **Elena Vasquez-Torres** --- individual, resident of Durham, North Carolina. Ms. Vasquez-Torres has approximately 22 years of commercial real estate development experience. Personal net worth: approximately \\$29,800,000.\n>\n> • **Reginald K. Osei** --- individual, resident of Chapel Hill, North Carolina. Mr. Osei has approximately 15 years of real estate finance and development experience. Personal net worth: approximately \\$11,500,000.\n\nCombined guarantor net worth: approximately \\$41,300,000.\n\n**1.4 Mezzanine Lender (Acknowledged)**\n\nThe Lender acknowledges that **Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC**, a North Carolina limited liability company (NC Secretary of State File No. 2103988), will provide subordinate mezzanine financing in the amount of **\\$9,200,000** in connection with the Project. The mezzanine loan shall be secured by a pledge of 100% of the membership interests in the Borrower. The mezzanine loan shall bear interest at a fixed rate of 12.50% per annum. The maturity date of the mezzanine loan shall be coterminous with the maturity of the senior Loan described herein, including any extension period, if applicable.\n\nAn intercreditor agreement between the Lender and the Mezzanine Lender is currently under negotiation and must be executed prior to or simultaneously with the closing of the Loan.\n\n**[Section 2 --- Project Description]{.underline}**\n\n**Project Name:** The Piedmont at Brightleaf\n\n**Property Address:** 601 and 615 Foster Street, Durham, Durham County, North Carolina 27701\n\n**Parcel IDs:** 0821-04-72-3341 and 0821-04-72-4102\n\n**Total Land Area:** 3.47 acres (combined two parcels)\n\n**Zoning:** MU-D (Mixed Use --- Downtown). The proposed development is permitted as of right under the current zoning designation. No special use permit, conditional zoning, or variance is required.\n\n**Current Condition:** Vacant improved land. The former tobacco warehouse structures on the site were demolished in August 2024. Environmental remediation of the site was completed in September 2024 in accordance with the applicable directives of the North Carolina Department of Environmental Quality (\\\"NCDEQ\\\").\n\n**Development Description:** The Project consists of the ground-up construction of a six (6)-story (five residential stories over one podium level), Class A mixed-use residential and retail development, together with an associated structured parking garage. The development program is summarized as follows:\n\n> • **Residential Unit Count:** 212 units, consisting of 142 one-bedroom units, 56 two-bedroom units, and 14 three-bedroom units\n>\n> • **Retail Space:** 18,400 square feet of ground-floor retail space across seven (7) retail bays\n>\n> • **Parking:** Four (4)-level structured parking garage with 276 spaces\n>\n> • **Total Gross Building Area:** 287,500 square feet\n>\n> • **Amenities:** Rooftop terrace, fitness center, co-working lounge, pool deck, and dog park\n\n**General Contractor:** Graystone Construction Group Inc., 1200 Fayetteville Road, Raleigh, North Carolina 27603 (NC General Contractor License No. 78442; President: Mark D. Sullivan). The construction contract is a guaranteed maximum price (\\\"GMP\\\") contract with a GMP amount of **\\$34,750,000**.\n\n**Project Architect:** Meridian Design Collective PC, a North Carolina professional corporation.\n\n**Projected Substantial Completion Date:** August 31, 2027.\n\n**[Section 3 --- Loan Terms]{.underline}**\n\n**3.1 Loan Amount**\n\n**\\$47,500,000** (Forty-Seven Million Five Hundred Thousand and 00/100 Dollars).\n\n**Loan Type:** Construction-to-mini-permanent loan. The Loan shall be structured as a single advance facility, with loan proceeds to be disbursed in accordance with the approved draw schedule set forth in Section 9 of this Term Sheet.\n\n**3.2 Loan Term**\n\n**Construction Period:** Thirty (30) months from the date of closing. Target closing date: February 28, 2025. Construction Maturity Date: August 28, 2027.\n\n**Mini-Perm Period:** Twelve (12) months following the Construction Maturity Date. Mini-Perm Maturity Date: August 28, 2028.\n\n**Extension Option:** One (1) six (6)-month extension of the Mini-Perm Period (the \\\"Extension Option\\\"), resulting in an Extended Maturity Date of February 28, 2029, subject to satisfaction of customary conditions to be determined and set forth in the definitive Loan Agreement.\n\n**3.3 Interest Rate**\n\n**Construction Period Rate:** Daily Simple SOFR + 3.25% per annum.\n\n**Mini-Perm Period Rate:** Daily Simple SOFR + 3.50% per annum.\n\n**SOFR Floor:** 1.00%, applicable to both the Construction Period and the Mini-Perm Period. If Daily Simple SOFR is less than 1.00% on any applicable business day, SOFR shall be deemed to be 1.00% for purposes of calculating the interest rate applicable to such day.\n\n**Default Rate:** The applicable contract rate plus 5.00% per annum.\n\nInterest shall be calculated on the basis of actual days elapsed over a 360-day year. Interest on the outstanding principal balance of the Loan shall be payable monthly in arrears on the first business day of each calendar month. During the Construction Period, interest shall be funded from the Interest Reserve (as described in Section 10 hereof) until the Interest Reserve is exhausted; thereafter, interest shall be payable by the Borrower from its own funds.\n\n\\\"Daily Simple SOFR\\\" means the Secured Overnight Financing Rate as published by the Federal Reserve Bank of New York (or a successor administrator) for the applicable business day. Benchmark replacement provisions consistent with the Alternative Reference Rates Committee\\'s recommended best practices shall be included in the definitive Loan Agreement, including customary benchmark replacement triggers, successor rate identification, and spread adjustments.\n\n**3.4 Fees. Origination Fee:** 1.00% of the Loan Amount = **\\$475,000**, payable in full at closing. The origination fee may be funded from Loan proceeds in accordance with the approved Project Budget.\n\n**Exit Fee:**\n\n> • 0.50% of the outstanding principal balance at the time of repayment if the Loan is repaid during the Construction Period;\n>\n> • 0.25% of the outstanding principal balance at the time of repayment if the Loan is repaid during the first six (6) months of the Mini-Perm Period;\n>\n> • No exit fee shall be payable if the Loan is repaid after the first six (6) months of the Mini-Perm Period.\n\n**Unused Line Fee:** 0.25% per annum on the average daily undrawn commitment amount, payable quarterly in arrears, commencing on the first quarterly date following closing.\n\n**[Section 4 --- Appraisal and Valuation]{.underline}**\n\nAn appraisal of the Property has been prepared by **Ridgeline Appraisal Services Inc.** (Appraiser: Linda M. Haverford, MAI), dated November 15, 2024, and has been reviewed by the Lender\\'s internal appraisal review department. The key valuation conclusions are summarized as follows:\n\n> • **\\\"As-Is\\\" Land Value:** \\$8,900,000\n>\n> • **\\\"As-Completed\\\" Appraised Value:** \\$72,800,000\n>\n> • **\\\"As-Stabilized\\\" Appraised Value (assumes 95% occupancy):** \\$76,200,000\n\n**Appraiser\\'s Projected Stabilized Net Operating Income:**\n\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Line Item**                                                   **Amount**\n  --------------------------------------------------------------- -----------------------------------\n  Residential Rental Income (212 units × avg. \\$2,245/mo. × 12)   \\$5,712,000\n\n  Retail Rental Income (18,400 SF × \\$30.00/SF NNN)               \\$552,000\n\n  Other Income (parking, amenities, etc.)                         \\$198,000\n\n  **Gross Potential Income**                                      **\\$6,462,000**\n\n  Less: Vacancy & Credit Loss (5.0%)                              (\\$323,100)\n\n  **Effective Gross Income**                                      **\\$6,138,900**\n\n  Less: Operating Expenses                                        (\\$1,262,100)\n\n  **Stabilized Net Operating Income**                             **\\$4,876,800**\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**Implied Capitalization Rate (As-Stabilized):** 6.40%\n\n**Loan-to-Value Ratios:**\n\n> • LTV (As-Completed): \\$47,500,000 ÷ \\$72,800,000 = **65.25%**\n>\n> • LTV (As-Stabilized): \\$47,500,000 ÷ \\$76,200,000 = **62.34%**\n\n**Projected Debt Service Coverage Ratio (Stabilized, Interest-Only):** Assuming a SOFR rate of 4.35% plus the Mini-Perm Period spread of 3.50%, the all-in interest rate would be 7.85% per annum, resulting in projected annual interest expense of approximately \\$3,728,750. Based on the Appraiser\\'s projected Stabilized NOI of \\$4,876,800, the projected DSCR is \\$4,876,800 ÷ \\$3,728,750 = **1.31x**.\n\nThe Lender\\'s maximum loan-to-value ratio shall not exceed 65% on an as-completed basis.\n\n**[Section 5 --- Sources and Uses / Project Budget]{.underline}**\n\n**5.1 Sources of Funds**\n\n  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Source**                                                   **Amount**\n  ------------------------------------------------------------ -----------------------------------\n  Senior Construction Loan (Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A.)       \\$47,500,000\n\n  Mezzanine Loan (Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC)            \\$9,200,000\n\n  Borrower Equity (land previously acquired; see Uses below)   \\$0\n\n  **Total Sources**                                            **\\$56,700,000**\n  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**5.2 Uses of Funds**\n\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Use**                                                               **Amount**\n  --------------------------------------------------------------------- -----------------------------------\n  Land Acquisition (previously closed)                                  \\$8,200,000\n\n  Hard Construction Costs (GMP --- Graystone Construction Group Inc.)   \\$34,750,000\n\n  Soft Costs (architecture, engineering, permits, legal, accounting)    \\$4,150,000\n\n  Interest Reserve                                                      \\$4,850,000\n\n  Loan Origination Fee                                                  \\$475,000\n\n  Developer Fee (5% of total project cost)                              \\$2,835,000\n\n  Contingency                                                           \\$1,440,000\n\n  **Total Uses**                                                        **\\$56,700,000**\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe land at 601 and 615 Foster Street was acquired by the Borrower prior to the closing of the Loan and is contributed to the Project as the Borrower\\'s equity. The land acquisition was funded from prior capital contributions by the Borrower\\'s members. The Borrower\\'s equity in the form of the previously acquired land will be reflected in the sources and uses analysis as the Borrower\\'s contribution to the Project capital stack. No additional cash equity contribution from the Borrower is reflected in the foregoing budget; however, the Borrower\\'s obligation to fund any cost overruns or interest reserve shortfalls from its own funds is set forth elsewhere in this Term Sheet.\n\n**[Section 6 --- Financial Covenants and Underwriting Requirements]{.underline}**\n\n**6.1 Loan-to-Cost Ratio**\n\nThe maximum Loan-to-Cost Ratio shall not exceed **80%** of Total Project Costs at any time during the term of the Loan. For purposes of this Section 6.1, \\\"Total Project Costs\\\" means the aggregate of all costs and expenses incurred or to be incurred in connection with the acquisition, development, construction, and completion of the Project, as set forth in the approved Project Budget. As of the date hereof, Total Project Costs are estimated at \\$56,700,000.\n\n**6.2 Loan-to-Value Ratios**\n\nThe maximum Loan-to-Value Ratio on an as-completed basis shall not exceed **65%**. The maximum Loan-to-Value Ratio on an as-stabilized basis shall not exceed **65%**. The foregoing LTV ratios are based on the appraisal dated November 15, 2024 by Ridgeline Appraisal Services Inc. and are subject to reappraisal at any time at the Lender\\'s discretion and at the Borrower\\'s expense.\n\n**6.3 Debt Service Coverage Ratio**\n\nThe minimum projected stabilized Debt Service Coverage Ratio shall be **1.25x**, based on interest-only debt service during the Mini-Perm Period. The DSCR shall be tested at the commencement of the Mini-Perm Period and annually thereafter based on actual trailing twelve-month net operating income. If at any time the DSCR falls below 1.25x, the Borrower shall, at the Lender\\'s election, either (a) make a principal curtailment sufficient to restore the DSCR to 1.25x or (b) fund a cash collateral reserve in an amount determined by the Lender.\n\n**6.4 Borrower Net Worth**\n\nThe minimum net worth of the Borrower shall be **\\$12,000,000**, tested annually. The current net worth of the Borrower is approximately \\$14,200,000, based on financial statements provided to the Lender.\n\n**6.5 Guarantor Liquidity**\n\nThe minimum combined liquidity of the Guarantors shall be **\\$5,000,000**, tested quarterly. Current combined guarantor liquidity is approximately \\$9,300,000, consisting of approximately \\$6,100,000 attributable to Elena Vasquez-Torres and approximately \\$3,200,000 attributable to Reginald K. Osei. For purposes of this requirement, \\\"liquidity\\\" means cash, cash equivalents, and marketable securities readily convertible to cash within thirty (30) days.\n\n**[Section 7 --- Guaranty]{.underline}**\n\n**7.1 Completion Guaranty**\n\nEach Guarantor shall execute and deliver a completion guaranty (the \\\"Completion Guaranty\\\") pursuant to which each Guarantor shall jointly and severally guarantee the lien-free completion of the Project in accordance with the approved plans and specifications, the approved Project Budget, and the construction schedule, on or before the Construction Maturity Date of August 28, 2027. The Completion Guaranty shall remain in full force and effect until the Lender has received satisfactory evidence that construction of the Project has been completed in all material respects, a final certificate of occupancy has been issued by the City of Durham, and all construction liens have been released or bonded off.\n\n**7.2 Carry Guaranty**\n\nEach Guarantor shall execute and deliver a carry guaranty (the \\\"Carry Guaranty\\\") pursuant to which each Guarantor shall jointly and severally guarantee the payment of interest and other carrying costs on the Loan during the term of the Loan. The Carry Guaranty is in addition to, and not in lieu of, the Interest Reserve described in Section 10 hereof. The Carry Guaranty shall apply to interest and carrying costs that accrue after the Interest Reserve has been exhausted or in the event that the Interest Reserve is insufficient to cover such costs.\n\n**7.3 Partial Repayment Guaranty**\n\nEach Guarantor shall execute and deliver a partial repayment guaranty (the \\\"Partial Repayment Guaranty\\\") in the amount of **25% of the Loan Amount** (25% × \\$47,500,000 = **\\$11,875,000**). The Partial Repayment Guaranty shall be joint and several, meaning that each Guarantor shall be individually liable for the full guaranteed amount. The Partial Repayment Guaranty shall be subject to customary \\\"bad boy\\\" carve-out provisions, including but not limited to fraud, misrepresentation, voluntary bankruptcy, unauthorized transfer, environmental liability, and waste, which may convert the Partial Repayment Guaranty to a full recourse obligation. Specific carve-out triggers and the circumstances under which the partial recourse guaranty may be converted to full recourse shall be set forth in the definitive Loan Agreement.\n\n**7.4 Environmental Indemnity**\n\nEach Guarantor shall execute and deliver an environmental indemnity agreement (the \\\"Environmental Indemnity\\\"), unlimited in amount, indemnifying the Lender against all environmental liabilities, losses, costs, damages, and expenses (including remediation costs, fines, penalties, and attorneys\\' fees) arising out of or related to the presence, release, or threatened release of any hazardous substances on, under, or from the Property. The Environmental Indemnity shall survive the repayment of the Loan, the release or reconveyance of the Deed of Trust, and any foreclosure or deed in lieu of foreclosure.\n\n**[Section 8 --- Collateral]{.underline}**\n\nThe Loan shall be secured by the following collateral:\n\n> • First priority Deed of Trust on the Property (Parcel IDs: 0821-04-72-3341 and 0821-04-72-4102; both parcels located at 601 and 615 Foster Street, Durham, North Carolina 27701), encumbering the fee simple interest in the Property, together with all improvements, fixtures, and appurtenances thereto;\n>\n> • First priority Assignment of Rents and Leases covering all current and future rents, revenues, and income from the Property;\n>\n> • First priority security interest in all personal property, fixtures, equipment, furniture, permits, plans, specifications, contracts, licenses, approvals, accounts, and general intangibles related to the Project;\n>\n> • Assignment of the construction contract (GMP contract with Graystone Construction Group Inc.), including all rights, claims, and benefits thereunder;\n>\n> • Assignment of the architect\\'s contract (Meridian Design Collective PC), including all architectural plans, drawings, and specifications;\n>\n> • Collateral assignment of all insurance proceeds and condemnation awards related to the Property and the Project;\n>\n> • Pledge of 100% of membership interests in the Borrower by all members (Elena Vasquez-Torres --- 62%; Brightleaf Investors Group LLC --- 28%; Reginald K. Osei --- 10%);\n>\n> • Such other collateral as the Lender may reasonably require in connection with the Loan.\n\n**[Section 9 --- Disbursement / Draw Schedule]{.underline}**\n\n**9.1 General Disbursement Provisions**\n\nLoan proceeds shall be disbursed in phases tied to construction milestones in accordance with the draw schedule set forth in Section 9.2 below. A **10% retainage holdback** shall apply to all hard construction cost disbursements. The retainage shall be held by the Lender and released only upon satisfaction of the conditions set forth below for Draw 9.\n\nEach draw request submitted by the Borrower must be accompanied by: (a) an updated construction progress report prepared by the Borrower and the general contractor; (b) a third-party construction inspector\\'s certification of the applicable milestone completion; (c) partial lien waivers from the general contractor and all subcontractors for work performed through the date of the draw request; (d) an updated title search or bring-down endorsement from Aldersgate Title & Escrow Inc. confirming the continued first-priority status of the Lender\\'s Deed of Trust and the absence of any intervening liens; and (e) evidence that all insurance coverages required under Section 19 remain in full force and effect.\n\nThe Lender reserves the right to conduct independent inspections of the Property and the Project prior to authorizing each draw, at the Borrower\\'s expense. The Lender shall use commercially reasonable efforts to process each draw request within ten (10) business days of receipt of a complete draw package.\n\n**9.2 Draw Schedule**\n\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Draw**          **Milestone**                                  **Cumulative % Complete**   **Amount**\n  ----------------- ---------------------------------------------- --------------------------- ------------------\n  1                 Closing (soft costs, interest reserve, fees)   0%                          \\$9,475,000\n\n  2                 Foundation Complete                            15%                         \\$5,212,500\n\n  3                 Structural Frame --- Level 3                   35%                         \\$6,950,000\n\n  4                 Structural Frame --- Topped Out                55%                         \\$6,950,000\n\n  5                 Building Envelope Complete                     70%                         \\$5,212,500\n\n  6                 MEP Rough-In Complete                          80%                         \\$3,475,000\n\n  7                 Interior Finish --- 50% Units                  90%                         \\$3,475,000\n\n  8                 Substantial Completion / TCO                   100%                        \\$3,475,000\n\n  9                 Retainage Release                              Post-CO                     \\$3,275,000\n\n  **Total**                                                                                    **\\$47,500,000**\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDraw 1 includes the origination fee (\\$475,000), the interest reserve (\\$4,850,000), and initial soft costs (\\$4,150,000). The retainage release (Draw 9) is subject to receipt of a final certificate of occupancy from the City of Durham and final unconditional lien waivers from the general contractor and all subcontractors.\n\n**[Section 10 --- Interest Reserve]{.underline}**\n\nThe Lender shall fund an interest reserve of **\\$4,850,000** from Loan proceeds at closing (the \\\"Interest Reserve\\\"). The Interest Reserve shall be held in a segregated sub-account of the construction loan (the \\\"Interest Reserve Account\\\") and shall be disbursed solely for the payment of interest accruing on the outstanding principal balance of the Loan during the Construction Period. Interest payments shall be made from the Interest Reserve Account on a monthly basis in accordance with the interest payment provisions set forth in Section 3.3 hereof, until such time as the Interest Reserve is exhausted.\n\nIn the event the Interest Reserve is insufficient to cover interest payments through the end of the Construction Period, the Borrower shall be obligated to fund any shortfall from its own funds within five (5) business days of written notice from the Lender. The adequacy of the Interest Reserve shall be assessed by the Lender periodically, no less than quarterly, during the Construction Period, and the Lender shall notify the Borrower of any projected deficiency.\n\n**[Section 11 --- Conditions Precedent to Closing]{.underline}**\n\nThe obligation of the Lender to close the Loan and make the initial advance of Loan proceeds shall be subject to the satisfaction or waiver of the following conditions precedent, each in form and substance satisfactory to the Lender and its counsel:\n\n> • Execution and delivery of definitive Loan Documents, including but not limited to the Loan Agreement, Promissory Note, Deed of Trust, Assignment of Rents and Leases, Security Agreement, Completion Guaranty, Carry Guaranty, Partial Repayment Guaranty, Environmental Indemnity Agreement, and Pledge Agreements;\n>\n> • Satisfactory completion of the Lender\\'s due diligence, including review of the following:\n>\n> • Appraisal by Ridgeline Appraisal Services Inc. (Linda M. Haverford, MAI), dated November 15, 2024, satisfactory to the Lender in all respects;\n>\n> • Phase I Environmental Site Assessment prepared by Sentinel Environmental Consulting LLC (Dr. James Whitfield, P.E.), dated October 28, 2024, and related Phase II investigation results, satisfactory to the Lender;\n>\n> • No Further Action letter from the North Carolina Department of Environmental Quality (\\\"NCDEQ\\\"), dated September 30, 2024, in form and substance satisfactory to the Lender;\n>\n> • Preliminary Title Commitment issued by Aldersgate Title & Escrow Inc. (Commitment No. NC-2024-88712, dated December 5, 2024) and issuance of a pro forma lender\\'s title insurance policy in an amount not less than the Loan Amount (\\$47,500,000), insuring the Lender\\'s Deed of Trust as a first-priority lien on the Property, subject only to Permitted Exceptions (as defined in Section 18 hereof);\n>\n> • ALTA/NSPS survey satisfactory to the Lender and the title company;\n>\n> • Execution and delivery of the construction contract (GMP contract with Graystone Construction Group Inc.) and the architect\\'s contract (Meridian Design Collective PC), in form and substance satisfactory to the Lender;\n>\n> • Receipt of all necessary governmental approvals, building permits, and zoning confirmations authorizing the construction and operation of the Project;\n>\n> • Borrower\\'s organizational documents, operating agreement, certificates of good standing from the North Carolina Secretary of State, and evidence of authority (including member resolutions authorizing the Loan and all transactions contemplated hereby);\n>\n> • Evidence of the financial condition of the Borrower and the Guarantors, including current financial statements, personal financial statements, and federal income tax returns for the prior two taxable years;\n>\n> • Evidence of insurance satisfactory to the Lender, including builder\\'s risk insurance (minimum \\$34,750,000), commercial general liability insurance (\\$5,000,000 per occurrence), and umbrella/excess liability insurance (\\$10,000,000);\n>\n> • Payment of the origination fee in the amount of \\$475,000;\n>\n> • Deposit of the Borrower\\'s required equity contribution, if any;\n>\n> • Legal opinions from Borrower\\'s counsel (Calloway & Strauss PLLC) as to due organization, valid existence, due authorization, enforceability of the Loan Documents, and such other matters as the Lender may reasonably require;\n>\n> • Execution of an intercreditor agreement between the Lender and Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC, in form and substance satisfactory to the Lender, governing the relative rights and priorities of the senior loan and the mezzanine loan;\n>\n> • Such other conditions, documents, and information as the Lender may reasonably require in connection with the closing of the Loan.\n\n**[Section 12 --- Representations and Warranties (Summary)]{.underline}**\n\nThe definitive Loan Agreement shall contain representations and warranties of the Borrower and the Guarantors that are customary for transactions of this type, including but not limited to the following:\n\n> • The Borrower is duly organized, validly existing, and in good standing under the laws of the State of North Carolina and has full power and authority to own the Property, conduct its business, enter into the Loan Documents, and perform all of its obligations thereunder.\n>\n> • The execution, delivery, and performance of the Loan Documents have been duly authorized by all necessary action on the part of the Borrower and its members, and the Loan Documents constitute the legal, valid, and binding obligations of the Borrower, enforceable in accordance with their respective terms.\n>\n> • There is no litigation, proceeding, investigation, or governmental inquiry pending or, to the Borrower\\'s knowledge, threatened against the Borrower, any Guarantor, or the Property that could reasonably be expected to have a material adverse effect on the Borrower, the Guarantors, the Property, or the Project.\n>\n> • The Property is in compliance with all applicable laws, ordinances, rules, regulations, zoning requirements, and environmental laws and regulations.\n>\n> • The financial statements of the Borrower and the Guarantors previously delivered to the Lender are true, complete, and accurate in all material respects and fairly present the financial condition of the Borrower and the Guarantors as of the dates thereof.\n>\n> • No default or event of default exists under any material agreement, instrument, or obligation to which the Borrower or any Guarantor is a party.\n>\n> • All permits, licenses, and approvals necessary for the construction and operation of the Project have been obtained or will be obtained prior to commencement of the applicable phase of construction.\n>\n> • The Borrower is a single-purpose entity with no assets, liabilities, or business operations other than those related to the ownership, development, construction, leasing, and operation of the Project.\n\nSpecific representations and warranties shall be set forth in the definitive Loan Agreement.\n\n**[Section 13 --- Affirmative Covenants (Summary)]{.underline}**\n\nDuring the term of the Loan, the Borrower shall comply with the following affirmative covenants, in addition to such other affirmative covenants as may be set forth in the definitive Loan Agreement:\n\n> • Maintain the Property in good condition and repair at all times;\n>\n> • Complete construction of the Project in accordance with the approved plans, specifications, and Project Budget on or before the Construction Maturity Date (August 28, 2027);\n>\n> • Provide the Lender with monthly construction progress reports, each accompanied by a certification from a third-party construction inspector engaged by the Lender;\n>\n> • Maintain all required insurance coverages in full force and effect at all times, including builder\\'s risk insurance (minimum \\$34,750,000), commercial general liability insurance (\\$5,000,000 per occurrence), and umbrella/excess liability insurance (\\$10,000,000);\n>\n> • Comply with all applicable laws, rules, regulations, and governmental requirements, including without limitation all environmental laws and regulations;\n>\n> • Maintain the Borrower\\'s status as a single-purpose entity in accordance with the requirements of Section 20 hereof;\n>\n> • Maintain a minimum net worth of \\$12,000,000, tested annually;\n>\n> • Cause the Guarantors to maintain combined minimum liquidity of \\$5,000,000, tested quarterly;\n>\n> • Provide annual audited financial statements of the Borrower and personal financial statements of the Guarantors within 120 days of the end of each fiscal year;\n>\n> • Promptly notify the Lender of any material adverse change in the financial condition of the Borrower or any Guarantor, or of any event or circumstance that could reasonably be expected to result in such a material adverse change;\n>\n> • Not modify the Project plans, specifications, or scope in any material respect without the prior written consent of the Lender; and\n>\n> • Comply with the terms and conditions of the intercreditor agreement with Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC.\n\nAdditional affirmative covenants to be included in the definitive Loan Agreement.\n\n**[Section 14 --- Negative Covenants (Summary)]{.underline}**\n\nDuring the term of the Loan, the Borrower shall not, without the prior written consent of the Lender, which consent may be withheld in the Lender\\'s sole and absolute discretion:\n\n> • Incur any additional indebtedness, whether secured or unsecured, other than the mezzanine loan from Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC (as permitted under this Term Sheet and the intercreditor agreement) and trade payables incurred in the ordinary course of business;\n>\n> • Create, incur, assume, or permit to exist any lien, encumbrance, security interest, or other charge upon the Property or any other collateral securing the Loan, other than Permitted Exceptions and the Lender\\'s own liens;\n>\n> • Sell, transfer, convey, assign, or otherwise dispose of the Property or any interest therein, whether directly or indirectly;\n>\n> • Change, modify, or otherwise alter the ownership structure or membership interests of the Borrower, including without limitation any transfer, pledge, encumbrance, or hypothecation of membership interests, subject to the mezzanine pledge as governed by the intercreditor agreement;\n>\n> • Amend or modify the Borrower\\'s operating agreement in any material respect;\n>\n> • Enter into any transaction with affiliates of the Borrower or any member thereof except on arm\\'s-length terms and for fair and reasonable consideration;\n>\n> • Make any distributions, dividends, or other payments to members during the Construction Period, except for payment of the developer fee in accordance with the approved Project Budget;\n>\n> • Amend or modify the construction contract with Graystone Construction Group Inc. or the architect\\'s contract with Meridian Design Collective PC in any material respect without the prior written consent of the Lender.\n\nAdditional negative covenants to be included in the definitive Loan Agreement.\n\n**[Section 15 --- Events of Default (Summary)]{.underline}**\n\nThe following shall constitute Events of Default under the definitive Loan Agreement (subject to applicable notice and cure periods as described below):\n\n> • Failure by the Borrower to pay any amount of principal, interest, fees, or other charges when due under the Loan Documents, subject to a five (5)-day grace period for monetary defaults;\n>\n> • Any representation or warranty made by the Borrower or any Guarantor in any Loan Document proves to have been untrue or misleading in any material respect when made;\n>\n> • Failure by the Borrower to observe or perform any non-monetary covenant or obligation under the Loan Documents, subject to a thirty (30)-day cure period for non-monetary defaults that are capable of cure; provided, however, that if such cure cannot reasonably be completed within thirty (30) days, and the Borrower is diligently pursuing such cure, the cure period shall be extended for an additional thirty (30) days;\n>\n> • Bankruptcy, insolvency, reorganization, or receivership of the Borrower, any Guarantor, or any member of the Borrower, whether voluntary or involuntary;\n>\n> • A material adverse change in the financial condition of the Borrower or any Guarantor, as determined by the Lender in its reasonable discretion;\n>\n> • Failure to achieve construction milestones within applicable timeframes to be specified in the definitive Loan Agreement (a \\\"Construction Delay Default\\\" shall be deemed to occur if the Project is more than ninety (90) days behind the approved construction schedule at any time during the Construction Period);\n>\n> • Abandonment of the Project by the Borrower or the general contractor;\n>\n> • Failure to maintain required insurance coverages;\n>\n> • Breach of any single-purpose entity covenant set forth in Section 20 hereof or the definitive Loan Agreement;\n>\n> • Default under the mezzanine loan documents or the intercreditor agreement (cross-default);\n>\n> • Any material violation of environmental laws or the issuance of any environmental order, directive, or lien affecting the Property;\n>\n> • Entry of one or more judgments in an aggregate amount exceeding \\$500,000 against the Borrower or any Guarantor that remains unsatisfied, unbonded, or unstayed for a period of thirty (30) days;\n>\n> • Any Guarantor\\'s net worth falls below the minimum threshold set forth in Section 6.4, or any Guarantor revokes, terminates, or disaffirms the guaranty or any obligation thereunder.\n\nSpecific Events of Default, together with related cure periods, notice requirements, and remedies, shall be fully set forth in the definitive Loan Agreement.\n\n**[Section 16 --- Remedies (Summary)]{.underline}**\n\nUpon the occurrence and during the continuance of an Event of Default, the Lender shall have the right, at its option and without further notice to the Borrower (except as required by applicable law), to exercise any or all of the following remedies:\n\n> • Accelerate the Loan and declare all outstanding principal, accrued and unpaid interest, fees, and other amounts immediately due and payable;\n>\n> • Cease making any further advances or disbursements under the Loan;\n>\n> • Exercise all rights and remedies available under the Loan Documents, including but not limited to foreclosure under the Deed of Trust in accordance with the laws of the State of North Carolina;\n>\n> • Apply the Default Rate (applicable contract rate plus 5.00% per annum) to all outstanding amounts;\n>\n> • Exercise all rights and remedies under the Guaranty agreements, including the Completion Guaranty, the Carry Guaranty, and the Partial Repayment Guaranty;\n>\n> • Exercise all remedies available under Article 9 of the Uniform Commercial Code of North Carolina with respect to personal property collateral and pledged membership interests.\n\nAll remedies of the Lender under the Loan Documents are cumulative and non-exclusive. No delay or failure by the Lender in exercising any right or remedy shall constitute a waiver thereof.\n\n**[Section 17 --- Environmental Matters]{.underline}**\n\nThe following environmental assessments and reports have been prepared in connection with the Property and reviewed by the Lender:\n\n> • **Phase I Environmental Site Assessment** prepared by Sentinel Environmental Consulting LLC (Dr. James Whitfield, P.E.), dated October 28, 2024.\n>\n> • **Phase II Environmental Investigation** completed August 2024 by Sentinel Environmental Consulting LLC.\n>\n> • **No Further Action (\\\"NFA\\\") Letter** issued by the North Carolina Department of Environmental Quality (\\\"NCDEQ\\\"), dated September 30, 2024.\n\nThe Phase I ESA identified a Recognized Environmental Condition (\\\"REC\\\") consisting of residual petroleum contamination from a former underground storage tank (\\\"UST\\\") on the northeast corner of Parcel 0821-04-72-4102. Contamination levels exceed NCDEQ residential soil standards but are below non-residential (commercial/industrial) standards. The NFA letter authorizes commercial use of the affected area (approximately 0.38 acres), conditioned on the installation and maintenance of a soil vapor mitigation system in the parking garage structure to be constructed on the affected portion of the site.\n\nThe Borrower shall comply with all conditions of the NFA letter, including the installation of the required soil vapor mitigation system, throughout the term of the Loan and thereafter for so long as such conditions remain in effect. The Borrower shall provide the Lender with evidence of installation and ongoing maintenance of the soil vapor mitigation system in accordance with the NCDEQ requirements. Any material non-compliance with the conditions of the NFA letter shall constitute an Event of Default under the Loan Documents.\n\n**[Section 18 --- Title and Survey]{.underline}**\n\nA Preliminary Title Commitment has been issued by Aldersgate Title & Escrow Inc. (Commitment No. NC-2024-88712, dated December 5, 2024; Escrow Officer: Patricia Langley) for the Property, consisting of Parcel IDs 0821-04-72-3341 and 0821-04-72-4102.\n\nThe Lender shall receive a lender\\'s title insurance policy in an amount not less than the Loan Amount (\\$47,500,000), insuring the Deed of Trust as a valid first-priority lien on the Property, subject only to the following Permitted Exceptions:\n\n> • Standard printed exceptions, to be removed or modified as required by the Lender;\n>\n> • Utility easement benefiting Duke Energy Carolinas along the western boundary of the Property (20-foot wide);\n>\n> • City of Durham stormwater management easement (recorded in Book 7421, Page 212, Durham County Registry) affecting approximately 0.22 acres in the southern portion of the site; and\n>\n> • Declaration of Covenants, Conditions, and Restrictions recorded in Book 6984, Page 1155, Durham County Registry, by the Brightleaf Historic District Association, Inc.\n\nAll other exceptions shown on Schedule B-II of the title commitment, including but not limited to any prior deeds of trust, shall be removed, released, or otherwise satisfied on or before the Closing Date, and the Lender shall receive evidence of such removal, release, or satisfaction in form and substance satisfactory to the Lender and its counsel.\n\nAn ALTA/NSPS Land Title Survey of the Property, prepared by a licensed surveyor registered in the State of North Carolina, satisfactory to the Lender and the title company, shall be delivered to the Lender and the title company prior to closing. The survey shall comply with the current ALTA/NSPS minimum standard detail requirements and shall include such Table A optional items as the Lender may specify.\n\n**[Section 19 --- Insurance Requirements]{.underline}**\n\nThe Borrower shall procure and maintain, at its sole cost and expense, the following insurance coverages during the term of the Loan:\n\n> • **Builder\\'s Risk Insurance:** In an amount not less than the total hard construction costs (\\$34,750,000), on an all-risk, replacement cost basis, naming the Lender as mortgagee and loss payee as its interests may appear;\n>\n> • **Commercial General Liability Insurance:** With minimum limits of \\$5,000,000 per occurrence and \\$10,000,000 in the aggregate, including coverage for premises liability, products/completed operations, contractual liability, and personal and advertising injury;\n>\n> • **Umbrella/Excess Liability Insurance:** With minimum limits of \\$10,000,000 per occurrence and in the aggregate, providing excess coverage above the commercial general liability policy;\n>\n> • **Workers\\' Compensation Insurance:** As required by the laws of the State of North Carolina, covering all persons employed in connection with the construction of the Project;\n>\n> • **Such Other Insurance** as the Lender may reasonably require, including flood insurance if the Property is determined to be located in a FEMA-designated Special Flood Hazard Area.\n\nAll policies shall name Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A. as additional insured and/or loss payee, as applicable. Evidence of insurance in form and substance satisfactory to the Lender shall be provided prior to closing and at each policy renewal during the term of the Loan. No policy shall be canceled, materially modified, or allowed to lapse without at least thirty (30) days\\' prior written notice to the Lender.\n\n**[Section 20 --- Single-Purpose Entity Requirements]{.underline}**\n\nThe Borrower shall maintain its status as a single-purpose entity (\\\"SPE\\\") at all times during the term of the Loan. The SPE covenants, to be fully specified in the definitive Loan Agreement, shall include the following requirements:\n\n> • The Borrower shall hold no assets other than the Property and related Project assets;\n>\n> • The Borrower shall incur no liabilities other than the Loan, the mezzanine loan (as permitted under this Term Sheet and the intercreditor agreement), and trade payables incurred in the ordinary course of business;\n>\n> • The Borrower shall conduct no business operations other than the ownership, development, construction, leasing, management, and operation of the Project;\n>\n> • The Borrower shall maintain separate books, records, financial statements, and bank accounts from those of any member, affiliate, or other entity;\n>\n> • The Borrower shall not commingle its funds or other assets with those of any member, affiliate, or other entity;\n>\n> • The Borrower shall hold itself out as a separate and distinct entity from its members and affiliates and shall conduct its affairs in its own name;\n>\n> • The Borrower shall observe all organizational formalities, including holding required meetings, maintaining required records, and making required filings with the North Carolina Secretary of State;\n>\n> • Such additional SPE covenants as may be required by the Lender in the definitive Loan Agreement, including without limitation the potential appointment of an independent manager or independent director to the Borrower\\'s governing body, whose affirmative vote shall be required for the Borrower to file a voluntary petition for bankruptcy or to take other specified actions.\n\n**[Section 21 --- Additional Provisions]{.underline}**\n\n**21.1 Reporting Requirements**\n\nThe Borrower shall provide the Lender with the following reports and financial information during the term of the Loan:\n\n> • Monthly construction progress reports, accompanied by a third-party construction inspector\\'s sign-off, within fifteen (15) days following the end of each calendar month during the Construction Period;\n>\n> • Quarterly unaudited financial statements of the Borrower, within forty-five (45) days following the end of each fiscal quarter;\n>\n> • Annual audited financial statements of the Borrower, prepared by a nationally or regionally recognized independent certified public accounting firm, within 120 days following the end of each fiscal year;\n>\n> • Annual personal financial statements of each Guarantor, within 120 days following the end of each fiscal year;\n>\n> • Quarterly guarantor liquidity certifications, in a form satisfactory to the Lender, within forty-five (45) days following the end of each fiscal quarter;\n>\n> • Annual borrower net worth certifications, in a form satisfactory to the Lender, within 120 days following the end of each fiscal year;\n>\n> • Copies of all material notices, permits, governmental correspondence, and regulatory communications related to the Property or the Project, promptly upon receipt thereof.\n\n**21.2 Lender\\'s Right to Inspect**\n\nThe Lender shall have the right to inspect the Property and the Project at any time during normal business hours upon reasonable prior notice to the Borrower. The Lender shall engage a third-party construction inspector, at the Borrower\\'s expense, to review and certify construction progress prior to each draw request and at such other times as the Lender may deem necessary in its reasonable discretion.\n\n**21.3 Assignment.** The Lender may assign, transfer, or participate its interest in the Loan, in whole or in part, without the consent of the Borrower. The Borrower may not assign or delegate its obligations under the Loan Documents, in whole or in part, without the prior written consent of the Lender, which consent may be withheld in the Lender\\'s sole discretion.\n\n**21.4 Governing Law**\n\nThe Loan Documents shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of North Carolina, without regard to its conflicts of law principles. The exclusive venue for any legal action or proceeding arising out of or related to the Loan or the Loan Documents shall be the General Court of Justice of North Carolina, Durham County, or the United States District Court for the Middle District of North Carolina, and each party irrevocably consents to the jurisdiction of such courts.\n\n**21.5 Expenses. The Borrower shall pay all costs and expenses incurred by the Lender in connection with the origination, documentation, closing, and administration of the Loan, including without limitation the legal fees and disbursements of Ashford, Cromdale Consulting & Laine LLP, appraisal fees, environmental assessment fees, title insurance premiums, survey costs, recording fees, construction inspection fees, and all other out-of-pocket costs and expenses. The Borrower shall be obligated to pay the Lender\\'s legal fees and expenses regardless of whether the Loan closes.**\n\n**[Section 22 --- Non-Binding Nature; Binding Provisions]{.underline}**\n\n**Non-Binding.** Except as expressly set forth below, this Term Sheet is a non-binding indication of the proposed terms and conditions of the Loan and does not constitute a legally binding commitment, agreement, or obligation on the part of the Lender to make the Loan or on the part of the Borrower to accept the Loan. All terms described herein (other than the Binding Provisions set forth below) are subject to: (a) satisfactory completion of the Lender\\'s due diligence, (b) approval of the definitive Loan Documents by the Lender and its counsel, (c) approval by the Lender\\'s Senior Loan Committee (if not previously obtained), and (d) no material adverse change in the financial condition of the Borrower or the Guarantors or in general real estate market conditions.\n\n**Binding Provisions.** Notwithstanding the foregoing, the following provisions shall be legally binding upon the parties upon execution of this Term Sheet:\n\n> • **Confidentiality.** Each party shall maintain the confidentiality of this Term Sheet and the terms, conditions, and financial information described herein, and shall not disclose the same to any third party without the prior written consent of the other party, except (i) to such party\\'s officers, employees, directors, members, legal counsel, accountants, and financial advisors who have a need to know such information in connection with the proposed transaction and who are bound by obligations of confidentiality, (ii) as required by applicable law, regulation, or legal process, or (iii) to the Mezzanine Lender to the extent necessary in connection with the negotiation of the intercreditor agreement.\n>\n> • **Exclusivity.** For a period of sixty (60) days from the date hereof (through and including March 11, 2025), the Borrower shall not, directly or indirectly, solicit, negotiate, or enter into any commitment, agreement, or term sheet for alternative construction financing for the Project from any other lender or financial institution.\n>\n> • Expense Deposit. The Borrower shall deposit \\$75,000 with the Lender upon execution of this Term Sheet as a non-refundable expense deposit, which shall be applied toward the Lender\\'s out-of-pocket costs and expenses incurred in connection with the proposed transaction, including without limitation the legal fees and disbursements of Ashford, Cromdale Consulting & Laine LLP. Any unused portion of the expense deposit shall be applied to the Borrower\\'s obligation to pay the Lender\\'s costs and expenses at closing; if the Loan does not close for any reason, any unused portion of the expense deposit shall be returned to the Borrower, net of expenses incurred through the date of termination.\n\nThis Term Sheet supersedes all prior discussions, negotiations, correspondence, and understandings between the parties with respect to the proposed Loan.\n\n**[Section 23 --- Acceptance and Execution]{.underline}**\n\nIf the foregoing terms and conditions are acceptable, please indicate your acceptance by signing this Term Sheet in the space provided below and returning an executed copy to the undersigned, together with the non-refundable expense deposit of \\$75,000 (payable by wire transfer to an account designated by the Lender), no later than **January 17, 2025**.\n\nThis Term Sheet shall automatically expire and be of no further force or effect if not accepted and returned with the expense deposit by **5:00 p.m. Eastern Time on January 17, 2025**.\n\nThe definitive Loan Documents will be prepared by the Lender\\'s counsel, Ashford, Cromdale Consulting & Laine LLP, and submitted to the Borrower\\'s counsel, Calloway & Strauss PLLC, for review and comment. Closing of the Loan is targeted for February 28, 2025, subject to the satisfaction of the conditions set forth herein and in the definitive Loan Documents.\n\nWe look forward to working with you on this transaction. Please do not hesitate to contact the undersigned with any questions.\n\n**LENDER:**\n\nPINNACLE SAVINGS BANK, N.A.\n\nBy: **\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_**\n\nName: David Forsythe\n\nTitle: Senior Vice President, Commercial Real Estate Lending\n\nDate: January 10, 2025\n\n**ACCEPTED AND AGREED:**\n\n**BORROWER:**\n\nHARBORVIEW CAPITAL PARTNERS LLC\n\nBy: **\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_**\n\nName: Elena Vasquez-Torres\n\nTitle: Managing Member\n\nDate: January 10, 2025\n\n**[Exhibit A --- Legal Description of the Property]{.underline}**\n\nSee attached legal descriptions for Parcel 0821-04-72-3341 (601 Foster Street, Durham, NC 27701) and Parcel 0821-04-72-4102 (615 Foster Street, Durham, NC 27701).\n\n*\\[Legal descriptions to be provided by Aldersgate Title & Escrow Inc. and confirmed by survey prior to closing.\\]*\n\n**[Exhibit B --- Organizational Chart of Borrower]{.underline}**\n\nSee attached organizational chart of Harborview Capital Partners LLC showing the ownership structure, including:\n\n> • **Elena Vasquez-Torres** --- 62% membership interest (Managing Member)\n>\n> • **Brightleaf Investors Group LLC** --- 28% membership interest (NC Secretary of State File No. 2045612; Managing Member: Thomas R. Chen)\n>\n> • **Reginald K. Osei** --- 10% membership interest\n\nNote: Brightleaf Investors Group LLC is under common control with Brightleaf Mezzanine Capital LLC (NC Secretary of State File No. 2103988), the Mezzanine Lender acknowledged in Section 1.4 of this Term Sheet.\n\n*\\[Full organizational chart to be provided by Borrower prior to closing.\\]*\n\n**[Exhibit C --- Project Budget Summary]{.underline}**\n\nSee attached Project Budget Summary prepared by the Borrower. Summary of Total Project Costs:\n\n  -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Line Item**                       **Amount**\n  ----------------------------------- -----------------------------------\n  Land Acquisition                    \\$8,200,000\n\n  Hard Construction Costs (GMP)       \\$34,750,000\n\n  Soft Costs                          \\$4,150,000\n\n  Interest Reserve                    \\$4,850,000\n\n  Loan Origination Fee                \\$475,000\n\n  Developer Fee                       \\$2,835,000\n\n  Contingency                         \\$1,440,000\n\n  **Total Project Costs**             **\\$56,700,000**\n  -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n*\\[Detailed budget and draw schedule to be provided by Borrower and approved by Lender prior to closing.\\]*\n\nCONFIDENTIAL --- This Term Sheet and its contents are confidential and proprietary to Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A. and Harborview Capital Partners LLC. Unauthorized reproduction or distribution is strictly prohibited. Bank Internal Loan Number: CRE-2025-0342.\n", "tool_call_id": "call_00_rJYAo7hLJjN9pIGhCcav0274", "tool_name": "read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"documents/executed-term-sheet.docx\"}"}
