r inquiry.\n\n**[SCHEDULE A --- POLICY INFORMATION]{.underline}**\n\n**Commitment Number: NC-2024-88712**\n\n**1. Effective Date of Commitment:** December 5, 2024, at 8:00 a.m.\n\n**2. Commitment Number:** NC-2024-88712\n\n**3. Policy or Policies to be issued:**\n\n> **(a) ALTA Loan Policy (06-17-06)**\n>\n> **Proposed Insured:** Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A., a nationally chartered savings bank, its successors and/or assigns\n>\n> **Proposed Policy Amount:** \\$47,500,000.00\n>\n> **Premium:** To be calculated at closing in accordance with the Company\\'s applicable rate schedule then in effect.\n>\n> **(b) ALTA Owner\\'s Policy (06-17-06)**\n>\n> **Proposed Insured:** Harborview Capital Partners LLC, a North Carolina limited liability company\n>\n> **Proposed Policy Amount:** \\$8,900,000.00 (based on as-is land value)\n>\n> **Premium:** To be calculated at closing in accordance with the Company\\'s applicable rate schedule then in effect.\n\n**4. The estate or interest in the Land described or referred to in this Commitment is:** Fee Simple\n\n**5. Title to the Fee Simple estate or interest in the Land is at the Effective Date hereof vested in:**\n\n> **Harborview Capital Partners LLC**, a North Carolina limited liability company (NC Secretary of State File No. 1923847)\n>\n> Title vested by Special Warranty Deed recorded in Book 7598, Page 443, Durham County Registry, dated June 12, 2023, from Foster Street Properties LLC, a North Carolina limited liability company, to Harborview Capital Partners LLC, a North Carolina limited liability company.\n\n**6. The Land referred to in this Commitment is described as follows:**\n\n> **Parcel 1 (PIN: 0821-04-72-3341):**\n>\n> Being all of that certain lot, tract, or parcel of land situated in the City of Durham, Durham County, North Carolina, and being more particularly described as follows:\n>\n> BEGINNING at an existing iron pipe located in the eastern right-of-way margin of Foster Street (60-foot public right-of-way), said iron pipe being located South 02°14\\'33\\\" West, 312.47 feet from the intersection of the eastern right-of-way margin of Foster Street with the southern right-of-way margin of West Corporation Street; running thence from said Beginning point along the eastern right-of-way margin of Foster Street, South 02°14\\'33\\\" West, 298.62 feet to an existing iron pipe; thence departing said right-of-way margin, South 87°45\\'27\\\" East, 305.41 feet to an existing iron pipe; thence North 02°14\\'33\\\" East, 298.62 feet to an existing iron pipe; thence North 87°45\\'27\\\" West, 305.41 feet to the point and place of BEGINNING; containing approximately 2.09 acres as shown on that survey plat recorded in Plat Book 218, Page 47, Durham County Registry.\n>\n> Being the same property conveyed to Harborview Capital Partners LLC by Special Warranty Deed recorded in Book 7598, Page 443, Durham County Registry.\n>\n> **Address:** 601 Foster Street, Durham, NC 27701\n>\n> **Containing approximately 2.09 acres.**\n>\n> **Parcel 2 (PIN: 0821-04-72-4102):**\n>\n> Being all of that certain lot, tract, or parcel of land situated in the City of Durham, Durham County, North Carolina, and being more particularly described as follows:\n>\n> BEGINNING at an existing iron pipe located in the eastern right-of-way margin of Foster Street (60-foot public right-of-way), said iron pipe being the southwestern corner of Parcel 1 described above; running thence from said Beginning point along the eastern right-of-way margin of Foster Street, South 02°14\\'33\\\" West, 201.88 feet to a new iron pipe; thence departing said right-of-way margin, South 87°45\\'27\\\" East, 297.63 feet to a new iron pipe; thence North 02°14\\'33\\\" East, 201.88 feet to an existing iron pipe, being the southeastern corner of Parcel 1 described above; thence along the southern boundary of Parcel 1, North 87°45\\'27\\\" West, 297.63 feet to the point and place of BEGINNING; containing approximately 1.38 acres as shown on that survey plat recorded in Plat Book 218, Page 48, Durham County Registry.\n>\n> Being the same property conveyed to Harborview Capital Partners LLC by Special Warranty Deed recorded in Book 7598, Page 445, Durham County Registry.\n>\n> **Address:** 615 Foster Street, Durham, NC 27701\n>\n> **Containing approximately 1.38 acres.**\n>\n> **Total combined land area: approximately 3.47 acres.**\n\n**7. Zoning:** According to the records of the City of Durham Planning Department, the Land is currently zoned **MU-D (Mixed Use --- Downtown)** under the City of Durham Unified Development Ordinance. The Company makes no representation as to compliance with applicable zoning ordinances or regulations.\n\n**[SCHEDULE B --- PART I: REQUIREMENTS]{.underline}**\n\n**Commitment Number: NC-2024-88712**\n\nThe following requirements must be met prior to issuance of the policy or policies described in Schedule A:\n\n**1. Payment to Aldersgate Title & Escrow Inc. of the applicable premiums, fees, and charges for the policy or policies to be issued, in accordance with the Company\\'s applicable rate schedule in effect at the time of closing.**\n\n**2.** Delivery of instruments creating the estate or interest to be insured, in form satisfactory to the Company, duly executed, acknowledged, and delivered for recording, including:\n\n> **(a)** Deed of Trust, Assignment of Rents, Security Agreement, and Fixture Filing from Harborview Capital Partners LLC, as Grantor, to a trustee satisfactory to the Company for the benefit of Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A., as Beneficiary, securing indebtedness in the principal amount of \\$47,500,000.00, duly executed, acknowledged, and recorded in the Durham County Registry.\n>\n> **(b)** UCC Financing Statement (Form UCC-1) filed with the North Carolina Secretary of State and/or the Durham County Registry, as applicable, naming Harborview Capital Partners LLC as Debtor and Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A. as Secured Party, covering all fixtures and personal property described in the security instruments.\n\n**3.** Evidence satisfactory to the Company that Harborview Capital Partners LLC is a limited liability company duly organized, validly existing, and in good standing under the laws of the State of North Carolina, and that the person or persons executing the insured instruments on behalf of said entity are duly authorized to do so. Required documents include:\n\n> **(a)** Certificate of Existence and/or Good Standing from the North Carolina Secretary of State, dated within thirty (30) days of the date of closing.\n>\n> **(b)** Certified copy of the Articles of Organization and Operating Agreement (or relevant excerpts thereof) of Harborview Capital Partners LLC, sufficient to identify the member(s) or manager(s) authorized to execute documents on behalf of the entity.\n>\n> **(c)** Resolution or written consent of the members of Harborview Capital Partners LLC authorizing the transaction contemplated herein and the execution and delivery of the loan documents and all ancillary instruments in connection therewith.\n\n**4.** Satisfaction and release of the Deed of Trust recorded in Book 6215, Page 892, Durham County Registry, from Harborview Capital Partners LLC (as successor-in-title to Foster Street Properties LLC, the original grantor) to Triangle Commercial Bank, dated September 14, 2018, securing an original indebtedness of \\$3,400,000.00. According to the public records of Durham County, no cancellation, release, or satisfaction of this instrument has been recorded as of the Effective Date. The Company requires either:\n\n> **(a)** A recorded Cancellation of Deed of Trust executed in accordance with N.C.G.S. § 45-37, or a Certificate of Satisfaction, in recordable form, duly executed by Triangle Commercial Bank or its successor or assign; or\n>\n> **(b)** A payoff letter from Triangle Commercial Bank or its successor or assign, dated within thirty (30) days of the date of closing, confirming the outstanding balance and per diem interest, with funds sufficient to pay such outstanding balance to be disbursed at closing through the Company\\'s escrow account, together with an indemnity agreement in form and substance satisfactory to the Company indemnifying the Company against loss arising from the failure to obtain and record a satisfaction or cancellation of said Deed of Trust.\n\n**5.** A satisfactory survey of the Land, prepared by a surveyor duly licensed in the State of North Carolina, certified to the Company, the Proposed Insured lender (Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A.), and the Proposed Insured owner (Harborview Capital Partners LLC), meeting the 2021 ALTA/NSPS Minimum Standard Detail Requirements for Land Title Surveys (including Table A optional items as requested by the parties), dated or re-certified within ninety (90) days of the date of closing.\n\n**6.** Evidence satisfactory to the Company that all real property taxes, special assessments, and governmental charges affecting the Land are paid current through the date of closing, with no delinquencies. According to Durham County Tax Administration records reviewed as of the Effective Date, the 2024 ad valorem tax bills for Parcel IDs 0821-04-72-3341 and 0821-04-72-4102 have been paid in full.\n\n**7.** Such other documents, instruments, certifications, affidavits, and information as may reasonably be required by the Company in connection with the issuance of the policy or policies described in Schedule A, including but not limited to affidavits of identity, lien waivers, gap indemnities, and closing instructions.\n\n**[SCHEDULE B --- PART II: EXCEPTIONS FROM COVERAGE]{.underline}**\n\n**Commitment Number: NC-2024-88712**\n\nThe policy or policies to be issued will contain exceptions to the following matters unless the same are disposed of to the satisfaction of the Company:\n\n**Standard / Printed Exceptions**\n\n**1.** Rights or claims of parties in possession not shown by the public records.\n\n**2.** Encroachments, overlaps, boundary line disputes, or other matters that would be disclosed by an accurate survey and inspection of the Land.\n\n**3.** Easements, or claims of easements, not shown by the public records.\n\n**4.** Any lien, or right to a lien, for services, labor, or material heretofore or hereafter furnished, imposed by law and not shown by the public records, including but not limited to mechanics\\' and materialmen\\'s liens arising under N.C.G.S. Chapter 44A.\n\n**5.** Taxes or special assessments which are not shown as existing liens by the records of any taxing authority that levies taxes or assessments on real property or by the public records. Proceedings by a public agency which may result in taxes or assessments, or notices of such proceedings, whether or not shown by the records of such agency or by the public records.\n\n**6.** Any service, installation, connection, maintenance, tap, capacity, or construction charges for sewer, water, electricity, natural gas, or garbage collection or removal affecting the Land.\n\n**NOTE:** Standard exceptions 1 through 3 above may be deleted upon receipt of a satisfactory current ALTA/NSPS survey meeting the requirements of Schedule B-I, Requirement No. 5, and an affidavit of possession from the vested owner in form satisfactory to the Company.\n\n**Special Exceptions. 7.** Ad valorem real property taxes for the fiscal year 2025 and subsequent years, which are a lien not yet due and payable. The 2024 ad valorem taxes for Parcel 1 (PIN: 0821-04-72-3341) were assessed at \\$29,847.12, and for Parcel 2 (PIN: 0821-04-72-4102) were assessed at \\$19,218.44, both of which have been paid in full.\n\n**8. Easement** in favor of Duke Energy Carolinas, LLC, for the installation, maintenance, repair, replacement, and operation of electric utility lines, poles, guys, anchors, and related facilities, being twenty (20) feet in width, running along the western boundary of Parcel 1 (PIN: 0821-04-72-3341), as set forth in that certain Easement Agreement recorded in Book 4387, Page 621, Durham County Registry, dated March 22, 1997. Said easement encumbers a strip of land approximately 20 feet in width measured from the western boundary line of Parcel 1 and extending easterly. This easement includes the right of ingress and egress to and from said facilities.\n\n**9. Stormwater Management Easement** in favor of the City of Durham, North Carolina, for the construction, operation, maintenance, inspection, and repair of stormwater management facilities, including drainage pipes, retention basins, and related infrastructure, affecting approximately 0.22 acres in the southern portion of Parcel 1 (PIN: 0821-04-72-3341), as set forth in that certain Stormwater Management Easement Agreement recorded in Book 7421, Page 212, Durham County Registry, dated April 8, 2022. The easement area is depicted on the plat recorded in Plat Book 232, Page 91, Durham County Registry.\n\n**10. Deed of Trust** from Foster Street Properties LLC (predecessor-in-title to the current vested owner, Harborview Capital Partners LLC) to the Trustee named therein for the benefit of Triangle Commercial Bank, dated September 14, 2018, recorded in Book 6215, Page 892, Durham County Registry, securing an original indebtedness in the principal amount of **\\$3,400,000.00**, together with all modifications, extensions, and renewals thereof, if any.\n\n> According to the public records of Durham County, no cancellation, release, satisfaction, or subordination of this Deed of Trust has been recorded as of the Effective Date of this Commitment.\n>\n> **NOTE from Title Officer:** The Borrower\\'s counsel, Calloway & Strauss PLLC (Jonathan F. Ngo), has advised the Company by correspondence dated November 22, 2024, that the indebtedness secured by this Deed of Trust has been partially repaid and that the remaining outstanding balance will be satisfied in full at or prior to closing from the Borrower\\'s own funds or from closing proceeds. The Company has not independently verified the outstanding balance of the secured indebtedness. The Company will require evidence of satisfaction or payoff as set forth in Schedule B --- Part I, Requirement No. 4, as a condition to deletion of this exception and issuance of the policy or policies described in Schedule A. Until such evidence is received and deemed satisfactory by the Company, this Deed of Trust will remain as an exception to the title policy.\n\n**11. Declaration of Covenants, Conditions, and Restrictions** (the \\\"Declaration\\\") recorded by the **Brightleaf Historic District Association, Inc.**, a North Carolina nonprofit corporation, in **Book 6984, Page 1155**, Durham County Registry, dated November 3, 2014, as amended by that certain First Amendment to Declaration of Covenants, Conditions, and Restrictions recorded in Book 7102, Page 388, Durham County Registry, dated June 19, 2017 (collectively, the \\\"Declaration\\\"). The Declaration imposes, among other things, the following obligations, restrictions, and encumbrances upon the Land:\n\n> **(a)** Architectural review and design standards requiring prior written approval from the Brightleaf Historic District Association Architectural Review Committee (the \\\"ARC\\\") for all new construction, exterior modifications, signage, landscaping plans, and exterior lighting on any parcel within the Brightleaf Historic District, as more particularly described in Article V of the Declaration.\n>\n> **(b)** Assessment obligations for the maintenance of common areas, shared infrastructure, and district-wide improvements, currently assessed at a rate of \\$0.12 per square foot of gross building area per annum, subject to annual adjustment by the Association Board of Directors, as set forth in Article VII of the Declaration.\n>\n> **(c)** Use restrictions consistent with the MU-D zoning classification applicable to the district, including the express prohibition of certain enumerated uses such as heavy industrial operations, automobile repair and service facilities, outdoor storage yards, adult entertainment establishments, and other uses as specified in Article IV, Section 4.3 of the Declaration.\n>\n> **(d)** A requirement that all development plans, including architectural drawings, site plans, grading plans, landscape plans, exterior material specifications, and signage designs, be submitted to the ARC no fewer than ninety (90) days prior to the anticipated commencement of construction, and that written ARC approval (or deemed approval upon the lapse of sixty (60) calendar days from the date of complete submission without written action by the ARC) be obtained as a condition to any building permit application with the City of Durham.\n>\n> **(e)** A right of the Association and/or any affected property owner within the Brightleaf Historic District to seek injunctive relief, including temporary restraining orders and preliminary and permanent injunctions, for violations of the Declaration, including a right to compel the cessation or halt of any construction that has not received ARC approval, as set forth in Article IX, Section 9.2 of the Declaration.\n>\n> **NOTE from Title Officer:** The Company has not received evidence that the current project plans for the proposed development known as \\\"The Piedmont at Brightleaf\\\" have been submitted to or approved by the Brightleaf Historic District Association Architectural Review Committee. Given the scope of the architectural review requirements and the Association\\'s right to seek injunctive relief, the Proposed Insured lender may wish to require evidence of ARC submission, ARC approval, or the expiration of the sixty (60) day deemed-approval period as a condition to closing and disbursement of loan proceeds.\n\n**12. Terms, conditions, easements, and restrictions** set forth in or imposed pursuant to the City of Durham Unified Development Ordinance and applicable zoning regulations for the MU-D (Mixed Use --- Downtown) zoning district, including but not limited to setback requirements, height restrictions, floor area ratio limitations, parking minimums and maximums, open space and common area requirements, public art installation requirements, and design overlay standards applicable to properties within the Downtown Development Tier.\n\n**13.** Any facts, rights, interests, or claims that are not shown by the public records but that could be ascertained by an inspection of the Land or that may be asserted by persons in possession of the Land or any portion thereof.\n\n> **NOTE:** This exception may be modified or deleted upon receipt of an acceptable affidavit of possession from the vested owner confirming that the Land is vacant and unoccupied, or occupied only by the vested owner, its agents, or its tenants under recorded leases, together with a satisfactory current survey as described in Schedule B --- Part I, Requirement No. 5.\n\n**[NOTES AND CONDITIONS]{.underline}**\n\n**Commitment Number: NC-2024-88712**\n\n**Note 1 --- Commitment Expiration.** This Commitment shall expire six (6) months from the Effective Date set forth in Schedule A (i.e., **June 5, 2025**) unless extended by written endorsement issued by the Company. Upon expiration, all liability of the Company under this Commitment shall cease and terminate, and this Commitment shall be of no further force or effect.\n\n**Note 2 --- Gap Coverage.** The Company will provide \\\"gap\\\" coverage for matters first appearing in the public records between the Effective Date of this Commitment and the date of recording of the insured instruments, subject to the Company\\'s standard gap indemnity requirements and the execution by the Proposed Insured of a gap indemnity agreement in form satisfactory to the Company.\n\n**Note 3 --- Insured Closing Letter. Upon request of the Proposed Insured lender or its counsel, the Company will issue an Insured Closing Letter (\\\"ICL\\\") confirming that Patricia Langley, as Escrow Officer of Aldersgate Title & Escrow Inc., is authorized to conduct the closing of the transaction described herein on behalf of the Company and in accordance with the Company\\'s written closing instructions.**\n\n**Note 4 --- Mechanic\\'s Lien Priority.** The Company notes that under North Carolina law (N.C.G.S. § 44A-10), a claim of lien on real property for furnishing labor or materials relates back to and is effective from the time of first furnishing of labor or materials at the site of the improvement. The Company recommends that the Proposed Insured lender require an affidavit from the vested owner and/or its general contractor confirming that no labor has been performed and no materials have been furnished to or incorporated into the Land prior to the recording of the insured Deed of Trust. In the event that any work has commenced or materials have been delivered to the Land prior to recording, the Company recommends that appropriate lien waivers from all contractors, subcontractors, and materialmen be obtained in form satisfactory to the Company.\n\n**Note 5 --- Environmental Matters.** This Commitment does not insure against loss or damage arising from or related to the presence, release, threatened release, or remediation of any environmental contamination, hazardous substances, pollutants, or conditions affecting the Land. Matters related to the North Carolina Department of Environmental Quality (NCDEQ) No Further Action letter dated September 30, 2024, and any prior environmental assessments, investigations, or remediation activities conducted on or affecting the Land, are outside the scope of this Commitment and of any policy to be issued hereunder.\n\n**Note 6 --- Contact Information.** All inquiries, document submissions, and correspondence regarding this Commitment should be directed to:\n\n> Aldersgate Title & Escrow Inc.\n>\n> Attn: Patricia Langley, Escrow Officer\n>\n> 307 West Chapel Hill Street, Suite 400 Durham, North Carolina 27701 Telephone: (919) 555-0174\n>\n> Email: plangley@crestviewtitle.com\n\n**END OF COMMITMENT**\n\nCommitment Number: NC-2024-88712 Effective Date: December 5, 2024, at 8:00 a.m. Issued by: Aldersgate Title & Escrow Inc.\n\nALDERSGATE TITLE & ESCROW INC.\n\nBy: **\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_**\n\nName: Patricia Langley\n\nTitle: Escrow Officer / Authorized Signatory\n\nDate: December 5, 2024\n", "tool_call_id": "call_01_BhqDxcSEGvTqK7xcWMR44766", "tool_name": "read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"documents/preliminary-title-commitment.docx\"}"}
