{"turn": 31, "role": "tool", "result": "1097:1. **Reconciliation.** $8,200,000 + $34,750,000 + $4,150,000 + $4,850,000 + $475,000 + $2,835,000 + $1,440,000 = $56,700,000. Senior Loan ($45,360,000) + Mezzanine Loan ($9,200,000) + Equity Deposit ($2,140,000) = $56,700,000.\n1099:2. **Loan-to-Cost.** Senior Loan ÷ Total Project Costs = $45,360,000 ÷ $56,700,000 = 80.00%, complying with Section 8.1. The Senior Loan commitment of $47,500,000 remains available for Advance if, when and to the extent Total Project Costs increase as approved by Lender under Section 4.7; in that event the Equity Deposit requirement is reduced correspondingly under Section 4.8(d).\n1101:3. **Equity allocation.** The Equity Deposit is allocated solely to Hard Costs, as required by Section 4.8(b), and may not be applied to the Developer Fee, the Interest Reserve, the Origination Fee or any Distribution.\n1103:4. **Land line item.** Line 1.01 is shown at the acquisition cost of $8,200,000 funded by the Mezzanine Loan in accordance with the Borrower's detailed budget. Lender's consent to the Mezzanine Loan does not constitute consent to any reimbursement of a Member's capital contribution; see Section 2.2, Section 4.16, Section 7.4 and Cover Memorandum Issue 3. Borrower must deliver the reconciled sources and uses statement required by Section 3.3(b) before Closing.\n1105:5. **Unbudgeted items.** The following recurring costs are not included in the Approved Budget and must be funded by Borrower from sources other than the Loan: the Unused Line Fee ($0.25% per annum), the Exit Fee, the Extension Fee, construction-period real property taxes (the 2024 combined tax bill for both parcels was $49,065.56), CC&R assessments (approximately $34,500 per annum), and audit fees.\n1107:6. **Interim true-up.** The allocation of Hard Costs between the Senior Loan and the Equity Deposit in the table is pro forma; the actual allocation will be determined as Advances are made, subject to Section 4.8.\n1148:1. **Reconciliation with the source draw schedule.** The draw schedule delivered by Borrower (dated January 8, 2025) presents the Advances in Part A in gross amounts (i.e., $5,212,500, $6,950,000, $6,950,000, $5,212,500, $3,475,000, $3,475,000 and $3,475,000) and describes the ninth advance of $3,275,000 as a \"Retainage Release,\" although 10% of the Guaranteed Maximum Price is $3,475,000 and the ninth advance is not sufficient to fund the retainage release. That schedule therefore neither withholds the stated 10% retainage nor funds the Developer Fee and Contingency, and its column components total $48,500,000 against a $47,500,000 commitment. This Schedule 1.2 restates the schedule on a net-of-retainage basis and reconciles it to the Commitment. The milestone percentages and gross Hard Cost amounts are unchanged from the source schedule. See Cover Memorandum, Issue 9.\n1150:2. **Timing.** The estimated dates are Borrower's projections and are not covenants; the outside date for Substantial Completion is governed by Section 6.1 and Section 10.7. Because the estimated date of the Final Advance (October 2027) falls after the Construction Maturity Date (August 28, 2027), the Final Advance may be made during the Mini-Perm Period, subject to the conditions in Section 4.4 and to no Event of Default then existing.\n1152:3. **Retainage.** Retainage shall be held by Lender and released only as part of the Final Advance. Lender may, at Borrower's request, permit reduction of Retainage to 5% upon the Construction Consultant's certification that the Project is 50% complete and satisfactory evidence that the Contractor's performance is on schedule and within budget, provided such reduction does not cause the LTC to exceed 80.00%.\n1223:1. The Advance is requested for Advance No. ___ under the Approved Draw Schedule and represents the milestone described as ____________________, which has been completed in accordance with the Approved Plans.\n1225:2. The proceeds will be applied solely to the following approved budget line items: ______________________________ (amount $__________), ______________________________ (amount $__________).\n1227:3. Attached hereto are: (a) AIA Forms G702 and G703 certified by the Architect and the Contractor; (b) the Construction Consultant's report; (c) conditional lien waivers from the Contractor and all subcontractors and materialmen through the date hereof; (d) the Title Company's date-down endorsement; (e) evidence of insurance; (f) the current Interest Reserve reconciliation demonstrating no Interest Reserve Deficiency; (g) the current budget reconciliation demonstrating sufficient remaining funds (including the undisbursed Commitment, the undisbursed Equity Deposit and available Contingency) to complete the Project; and (h) such other items as Lender has requested.\n1229:4. No Event of Default exists, and no event has occurred which, with notice or lapse of time or both, would constitute an Event of Default.\n1231:5. All representations and warranties in the Loan Documents are true and correct in all material respects as of the date hereof.\n1233:6. The Loan-to-Cost Ratio, after giving effect to this Advance, will not exceed 80.00%. It will equal ______%.\n1235:7. [If applicable] The conditions in Section 6.4(e) with respect to work in, over or adjacent to the Affected Area have been satisfied.\n1237:8. The Equity Deposit has been applied to Eligible Costs as required by Section 4.8 in the amount of $__________, and $__________ remains unapplied.\n---\n17\n", "tool_call_id": "call_00_jLMG573f0xe6jTXNWXIm5100", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR/work && grep -n '^[0-9]\\\\+\\\\. ' la.md | head -40; echo ---; grep -c '^[0-9]\\\\+\\\\. ' la.md\"}"}
