{"turn": 75, "role": "tool", "result": "  PRIVILEGED AND CONFIDENTIAL — ATTORNEY–CLIENT COMMUNICATION — ATTORNEY\n       WORK PRODUCT — PREPARED IN ANTICIPATION OF LOAN DOCUMENTATION\n\n\n                               MEMORANDUM\nTO:        David Forsythe, Senior Vice President — Commercial Real Estate Lending,\n           Pinnacle Savings Bank, N.A.; Senior Loan Committee (copy)\nFROM:      Katharine “Kate” Drummond, Partner; Marcus Webb, Associate — Ashford, Cromdale\n           Consulting & Laine LLP\nDATE:      February 3, 2025\nRE:        The Piedmont at Brightleaf — Loan No. CRE-2025-0342 — $47,500,000 Construction-\n           to-Mini-Permanent Loan — Transmittal of Draft No. 1 Loan Agreement and Schedule of\n           Material Issues, Inconsistencies and Recommended Resolutions across the Source\n           Document Record\n1. Purpose, scope and limitations of this review\n1.1 Purpose. You asked us to (a) prepare a first draft of the construction-to-mini-\npermanent loan agreement for the above transaction from the record described\nbelow, and (b) prepare this memorandum flagging material issues and\ninconsistencies across the source documents, with recommended resolutions. The\ndraft agreement is delivered with this memorandum as Construction-to-Mini-\nPermanent Loan Agreement — Draft No. 1.\n1.2 Record reviewed. We have read, in full, each of the seven documents listed in\nSection 2. Nothing else was in the workspace, and we have not reviewed any\ndocument outside that list. We have not obtained or reviewed: the Borrower’s\nfinancial statements or tax returns; the guarantors’ personal financial statements\n(only the summaries in the Credit Memorandum); the construction contract; the\narchitect’s agreement; the ALTA/NSPS survey; the operating agreement (only the\nexcerpts annexed to the Borrower’s organizational materials); the mezzanine loan\ndocuments; a draft intercreditor agreement; the NCDEQ No Further Action letter\nitself (only the summary and quotations in the Phase I ESA); the Phase II report;\nthe recorded deed notice; or the appraisal review memorandum. Each of these\ngaps is a diligence item, and several bear directly on conclusions in this\nmemorandum (see Section 8).\n1.3 Limitations. This memorandum is a summary of documentary inconsistencies\nand proposed resolutions, prepared for the Lender’s internal use. It is not a legal\nopinion on the enforceability of the draft, on title, on environmental liability or on\nregulatory capital treatment. Where the record contains a factual conflict that the\ndocuments cannot resolve, we have identified the conflict and stated what is\nneeded to resolve it rather than assuming an answer. Every figure in Section 5 has\nbeen recomputed independently from the underlying inputs; where our\nrecomputation differs from a stated figure, we say so and show the arithmetic.\n1.4 Format convention. “Term Sheet” means the executed term sheet dated\nJanuary 10, 2025; “Credit Memorandum” or “CM” means the Senior Loan\nCommittee credit memorandum dated January 22, 2025; “Appraisal” means the\nRidgeline Appraisal Services Inc. executive summary dated November 15, 2024\n(file RAS-2024-1147); “Title Commitment” means Aldersgate Title & Escrow\n\f                         Privileged & Confidential — Attorney–Client Communication — Attorney Work Product\n\n\n\nInc. Commitment No. NC-2024-88712 effective December 5, 2024; “Phase I ESA”\nmeans the Sentinel Environmental Consulting LLC excerpt dated October 28, 2024\n(project SEC-2024-1147); “Org Chart” means the Borrower organizational chart\nand operating agreement excerpts delivered by Calloway & Strauss PLLC in\nJanuary 2025; and “Draw Schedule” means the construction budget and draw\nschedule workbook prepared by the Borrower dated January 8, 2025. “Draft”\nmeans the accompanying Draft No. 1 Loan Agreement. Section references are to\nthe document named.\n2. Documents reviewed and what each establishes\nDocument               Date         Author / issuer          What it establishes for this review\n", "tool_call_id": "call_00_ET_tu1sT2ZkX6PgENWMkrbC9303", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR/work && pdftotext -layout -f 1 -l 2 pdfm/memo_formatted.pdf - | head -60\"}"}
