{"turn": 80, "role": "tool", "result": "tables: 7\nok\nOK: wrote memo_raw.docx\nsaved memo_formatted.docx\nPages:           29\n                         Privileged & Confidential — Attorney–Client Communication — Attorney Work Product\n\n\n\nappears to be inaccurate, which matters for the 62/28/10 allocation, the\ndistribution waterfall in operating agreement §6.1, and the truth of the\nrepresentation at Draft §5.16.\nMore significantly, the sources and uses presented to the Bank funds every dollar\nof a $56,700,000 budget — including the $8,200,000 land cost, which was paid in\n2023 — with debt: $47,500,000 senior plus $9,200,000 mezzanine. Because the\nland is already owned, the mezzanine proceeds allocated to line 1.01 can only be a\nreimbursement of whoever funded the land. If that reimbursement occurs at\nclosing: (a) the Borrower’s equity at risk is limited to the $2,140,000 Equity\nDeposit, i.e. approximately 3.8% of cost and 2.9% of as-completed value; (b) the\npayment is a return of capital to a member, which breaches Term Sheet §14 (no\ndistributions during the construction period except the developer fee); (c) the CM’s\nstatement that total equity “would consist of $2,140,000 in cash plus $8,200,000 in\nland … approximately 18.2%” (CM §5.3) double-counts the land, because the land\nhas been converted back into cash; and (d) the HVCRE contributed-capital\ncalculation at CM §12 (14.2%) is overstated on the same basis — the correct figure\non a cash-out structure is 2.94%, and even counting land at as-is appraised value\n($8,900,000) the 15.16% result depends on the land not being reimbursed. HVCRE\nclassification therefore appears unavoidable, and the 150% risk weighting the CM\nalready accepts will apply.\nRecommendation. (a) Require source-of-funds tracing for the original land\npurchase (closing statement, bank records, member capital account ledger). (b)\nRequire the Borrower to deliver a reconciled, certified sources and uses statement\nand a closing flow of funds that shows no payment to any member other than\napproved project costs (Draft §3.3(b)). (c) Retain the express prohibition on\nreimbursing member capital from any source at Draft §§2.2, 4.16 and 7.4. (d) If the\ncommercial intention is to cash out the land, the Bank should grant that relief\nknowingly, in writing, and re-underwrite the credit without the land credit —\nwhich would fail the HVCRE and equity tests as currently sized. (e) Correct the\nCM’s 18.2% and 14.2% figures before committee re-approval.\n\n", "tool_call_id": "call_00_XxCgdV2riVTA949do4AJ0467", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR/work && python3 - << 'EOF'\\ns=open('fixtables2.py').read()\\ns=s.replace(\\\"([1.75,1.10,2.30,1.35],'llll'),\\\",\\\"([1.40,0.95,2.65,1.50],'llll'),\\\")\\nopen('fixtables2.py','w').write(s)\\nEOF\\npython3 fixtables2.py && python3 $WORKSPACE_DIR/skills/docx/scripts/generate_from_md.py memo_fixed.md memo_raw.docx reference.docx && python3 post_memo.py memo_raw.docx memo_formatted.docx && rm -f pdfm/memo_formatted.pdf && timeout 240 soffice --headless --convert-to pdf memo_formatted.docx --outdir pdfm >/dev/null 2>&1; pdfinfo pdfm/memo_formatted.pdf|grep Pages; pdftotext -layout -f 11 -l 11 pdfm/memo_formatted.pdf - | head -35\"}"}
